# openOODA install system

## Source of truth

| Artifact | Role |
|---|---|
| **`install/install.oo`** | Full installer — story, XDG layout, download, place, config, verify |
| **Website `install` / `install.sh`** | Chapter 0 bootstrap only (fetch prebuilt binary, then hand off) |
| **`scripts/release.sh`** | Packages pure `bin/ooda` + `oodac` + `install/install.oo` + `share/` + runtime C; writes `.sha256` |
| **`scripts/bootstrap_no_cargo.sh`** | Rebuild pure product from seed + gcc |
| **`scripts/install_dress_rehearsal.sh`** | Offline layout dress rehearsal of release tarball / staged tree |
| **`bootstrap/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.oot`** | Pin lock + release notes habit (not beta gate) |

Shell cannot be eliminated for a **first** install (no `ooda` yet). Everything after that is OODA.

## XDG layout (after install.oo)

| Variable | Default | Contents |
|---|---|---|
| `OODA_HOME` | `$XDG_DATA_HOME/ooda` → `~/.local/share/ooda` | data: `std/`, `share/`, `install/` |
| `OODA_BIN` | `$XDG_BIN_HOME` → `~/.local/bin` | `ooda` binary on PATH |
| `OODA_CONFIG` | `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ooda` → `~/.config/ooda` | `env` shell snippet |
| `OODA_CACHE` | `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/ooda` → `~/.cache/ooda` | downloads + extract |
| `OODA_STD` | `$OODA_HOME/std` | **product** `ooda/std` (copied, not org `std/`) |
| `OODA_SRC_ROOT` | `$OODA_HOME` | `runtime/chs_rt.c` for emit+gcc |
| `OODA_VERSION` | pin e.g. `v0.186.0-alpha` | release tag to fetch |

## Interactions (honest)

The `.oo` installer does **not** ask yes/no. HITL is not product.
You grant writes by setting env, then it runs.

| You set | Why |
|---|---|
| `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR=$HOME` | `write_file` only writes under this prefix |
| `OODA_CHECKOUT=$PWD` | Checkout that already has `bin/ooda` and `oodac/oodac` |

No network. No TTY prompt. First machine with no compiler still needs `bootstrap/oodac_pure_build`.

## User commands

```bash
# Preferred: rebuild, then XDG install
cd ooda
OODAC_BIN=./bootstrap/seed/oodac bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
OODA_FS_WRITEDIR="$HOME" OODA_CHECKOUT="$PWD" ooda install
. ~/.config/ooda/env
oodac
ooda

# First machine with no ooda yet: host rebuild, then the same install
# The ooda GitHub repo is private, so a stranger cannot clone it.
```

## Release pack

```bash
./scripts/release.sh                 # pin from install/BOOTSTRAP_PIN
./scripts/release.sh v0.186.0-alpha
```

Pure product pack: requires seed + gcc to rebuild if binaries missing.
